_meanings:
²1 To sit near to (with <ab>acc.</ab>), sit at the side of (as a mark of submission
 and respect); wait upon, serve, worship; {#omityetadakzaramudgITamupAsIta#}
 <ls>Ch. Up. 1. 1. 1</ls> <ab>&c.</ab> {#mAM DyAyanta upAsate#} <ls>Bg. 12. 6</ls>, <ls n="Bg.">9. 14</ls>, <ls n="Bg. 9.">15</ls>. {#udyAnapAlasAmAnyamftavastamupAsate#}
 <ls>Ku. 2. 36</ls>; {#ambAmupAsva sadayAm#} <ls>Aśvad. 13</ls>; <ls>Śi. 16. 47</ls>; <ls>Ms. 3. 189</ls>.
.²2 To use, occupy, abide in, reside; {#EndraM sTAnamupAsInA brahmaBUtA#}
 {#hi te sadA#} <ls>Rām. 1. 35. 1</ls>; <ls>Ms. 5. 93</ls>.
.²3 To pass (as time); {#upAsya rAtriSezaM tu#} <ls>Rām.</ls>
.²4 To approach, go to or towards; {#upAsAYcakrire drazwuM devaganDarvakinnarAH#}
 <ls>Bk. 5. 107</ls>; {#paralokamupAsmahe#} <ls n="Bk.">7. 89</ls>.
.²5 To invest or blockade (as an enemyʼs town).
.²6 To be intent upon, be engaged in, take part in, (perform as a sacred
 rite); {#upAsya paScimAM sanDyAm#} <ls>K. 176</ls>, <ls n="K.">179</ls>; {#tepyupAsantu me maKam#}
 <ls>Mb.</ls>; <ls>Ms. 2. 222</ls>, <ls n="Ms.">3. 104</ls>, <ls n="Ms.">7. 223</ls>, <ls n="Ms.">11. 42</ls>.
.²7 To undergo, suffer; {#alaM te pARquputrARAM BaktyA kleSamupAsitum#}
 <ls>Mb.</ls>; <ls>Ms. 11. 184</ls>.
.²8 To remain or continue in any state or action; <ab>oft.</ab> with a {%<ab>pres. p.</ab>%};
 {#ananyenEva yogena mAM DyAyanta upAsate#} <ls>Bg. 12. 6</ls>.
.²9 To expect, wait for; {#dizwamupAsInaH#} <ls>Mb.</ls>
.²10 To attach

 oneself to, practise; {#upAsate dvijAH satyam#} <ls>Y. 3. 192</ls>.
.²11 To resort to, employ, apply, use; {#lakzaRopAsyate yasya kfte#} <ls>S. D. 2</ls>;
 {#bastirupAsyamAnaH#} <ls>Suśr.</ls>
.²12 To respect, recognize, acknowledge.
.²13 To practise archery.
